Guard ext/dom's xmlHashScanner callback the way php-src itself does from 7.1 on.

libxml2 2.9.8 added `const` to the `name` parameter of xmlHashScanner:

    void (*xmlHashScanner)(void *payload, void *data, const xmlChar *name);

php-src fixed this in 7.1 (ext/dom/dom_iterators.c) with a LIBXML_VERSION guard
that picks the const signature on 2.9.8 and newer; 7.0 never received the
backport and still declares itemHashScanner with a plain `xmlChar *name`. On
trixie (libxml2 2.9.14, LIBXML_VERSION 20914) the two xmlHashScan() call sites
therefore pass a function pointer whose type does not match the parameter, which
clang 16 and newer report as -Wincompatible-function-pointer-types -- an error
by default, not a warning.

This is a diagnostics-only mismatch (const qualification on a pointer parameter,
identical ABI on every platform this image targets), so it could equally be
silenced with -Wno-incompatible-function-pointer-types. It is patched instead
because a -Wno- flag applies to the whole tree for the whole compile, and this
build deliberately keeps `make` strict so a real pointer bug in php-src still
fails: see php/build.sh's CONFIGURE_ONLY_CFLAGS/MAKE_ONLY_CFLAGS split. The
patch is 7.0-only -- 7.1 through 8.0 already carry this exact guard upstream.

Verbatim backport of the 7.1.33 form of the same function.

--- a/ext/dom/dom_iterators.c
+++ b/ext/dom/dom_iterators.c
@@ -42,7 +42,11 @@
 	xmlNotation *notation;
 };
 
-static void itemHashScanner (void *payload, void *data, xmlChar *name) /* {{{ */
+#if LIBXML_VERSION >= 20908
+static void itemHashScanner (void *payload, void *data, const xmlChar *name) /* {{{ */
+#else
+static void itemHashScanner (void *payload, void *data, xmlChar *name)
+#endif
 {
 	nodeIterator *priv = (nodeIterator *)data;
 
